nged pass record is accepted only against its first parent when its nine-key grammar is complete, its delta is none or within and is the plan's own line, its digests match the parent's plan and Done-when, its cited critique is byte-identical in that parent, bound to its reviewed commit and accepted by the verdict grammar, and its dispute pair is both present or both empty; a cited critique record is only round one or round two, and any other round is no record. A second-round non-approval additionally requires an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking and major finding. At filing and commit creation, the reviewed tree also holds the bound plan bytes and Done-when digest. The gate judges the staged lane change, squash-carried lane commits, and landing lane commits oldest first; a squashed tip that no local branch contains is held by name while the landing tree carries any single or out-of-set claim copy; it compares a merge with every parent and holds unreadable claim copies, diffs, listings, records or parents. Trunk and a lane with no single row are not gated. The Done-when digest a record binds is unmoved by a tick or evidence on a Done-when item, so neither unbinds the record.\""," rationale = \"A single-plan item needs one durable, fail-closed release boundary so a skipped hook, rebase, merge or landing cannot turn an unreviewed plan into build output.\""," test_refs = \"TC-367\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-913\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3549,"oldLines":5,"newStart":3549,"newLines":5,"lines":[" expected = \"Build output is held at each gate until a supported pass record binds it, and a changed plan or Done-when unbinds it while a tick does not. Unsupported records hold. Record homes and a valid close pass before a record. A rebase preserves a binding and a merge is judged only for its own changes. Only the lane's claimed copy controls the closed planmode set: absent, empty, none and dual do not hold; single and every other value do. Trunk and a lane without a single-plan row are not held. A non-string mark and an unattributed squash hold by name, and a critique round past the cap is no record. The shipped hook step list refuses unplanned build output by the gate's name. A log fragment, and a refresh merge's compiled log and regenerated views, pass before a record; a regenerated view written outside a merge is build output. A pass form or pass-record commit whose critique reviewed another Done-when digest is refused. A pass record renders and reads through one exact grammar; partial, extra-keyed or field-invalid records are malformed, and its delta is one typed line from none, within or beyond. A critique record outside its own plan home, or past the cap, is no record.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_build_without_a_pass_record_is_refused_at_the_hook_and_the_landing; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_build_after_its_pass_record_is_not_refused_anywhere; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_the_merge_slot_asks_the_gate_of_each_lane_commit; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_plan_edited_after_its_record_is_refused_until_a_new_record_binds_it; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_done_when_edit_unbinds_and_a_tick_does_not; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_absent_unreadable_and_malformed_records_hold; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_record_naming_another_row_or_digest_holds; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_pass_record_committed_with_its_critique_is_refused_and_the_two_commit_order_passes; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_pass_record_whose_digests_its_parent_does_not_support_is_refused; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_pass_record_whose_critique_reviewed_another_plan_is_refused; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_a_pass_record_whose_critique_reviewed_another_done_when_is_refused; tests/test_plan_gate.py::test_the_shipped_hooks_floor_refuses_an